# standard.memory.semsig — generated signature sidecar (README §8, §29 #14).
# The SAFE allocator/region API agents allocate through (WS1-118): regions, views,
# owned buffers, and the allocator-as-capability model. Raw c.malloc/c.free is a
# stdlib-internal `unsafe` binding (WS1-116) — never app source. The in-language
# impl is the `region` construct (WS1-112): `allocateIn`/`releaseRegion` lower to a
# real arena (malloc-many / free-once) and JIT-run; this contract documents the
# types + capabilities the linter checks (allocate needs a capability, SS1563).

memorySig is semsig
memorySig version "1.0"
memorySig generatedBy "semanticscript 0.1"
memorySig describes standard.memory

Region is alias
Region for OpaquePointer
Region purpose "An allocation arena; everything allocated in it is freed once at releaseRegion"

View is alias
View for OpaquePointer
View purpose "A non-owning view of memory allocated in a Region (borrows the region's lifetime)"

OwnedBuffer is alias
OwnedBuffer for OpaquePointer
OwnedBuffer purpose "A heap buffer owned by the caller, released by memory.releaseBuffer"

ByteCount is alias
ByteCount for Int64
ByteCount purpose "A size/length in bytes"

AllocationFailure is error
AllocationFailure purpose "Out-of-memory / capacity-exceeded from an allocator"

# The allocator capabilities are declared app-side, not in this sidecar (a .semsig
# carries only intrinsics + the types they reference): the app grants
# `allocate heap.<region>` / `free heap.<region>` and `uses` them (SS1563).

memoryOpenRegion is intrinsic
memoryOpenRegion target memory.openRegion
memoryOpenRegion arg strategy String
memoryOpenRegion arg capacity ByteCount
memoryOpenRegion out region Region
memoryOpenRegion catch AllocationFailure
memoryOpenRegion owns region
memoryOpenRegion cleanedBy memory.releaseRegion
memoryOpenRegion purpose "Open an allocation region (arena|fixedBuffer|general); released by memory.releaseRegion (deferred runtime — the `region` construct is the in-language form)"

memoryAllocateIn is intrinsic
memoryAllocateIn target memory.allocateIn
memoryAllocateIn arg region Region
memoryAllocateIn arg bytes ByteCount
memoryAllocateIn out view View
memoryAllocateIn catch AllocationFailure
memoryAllocateIn borrows region
memoryAllocateIn lifetime region
memoryAllocateIn mayEscape no
memoryAllocateIn purpose "Allocate `bytes` in the region, returning a View that borrows it (deferred runtime)"

memoryReleaseRegion is intrinsic
memoryReleaseRegion target memory.releaseRegion
memoryReleaseRegion arg region Region
memoryReleaseRegion out released Int32
memoryReleaseRegion purpose "Free the whole region at once (every View into it becomes invalid) (deferred runtime)"
